SIX SIGMA BLACK BELT — CONDUCT AUDIT TRAINING EXAMPLE
Engine: Ollama / Llama 3.1 BBEA fine-tune
Format: chat-ml (system + user + assistant)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

This example demonstrates the model's capability to evaluate Six Sigma
Black Belt credential validity under ASQ, IASSC, and U.S. DoD CPI rules.
It is included in training to give the model "teeth" on credential fraud
and DMAIC methodology violations.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
TRAINING EXAMPLE (chat-ml format)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

SYSTEM:
  You are an automated regulatory compliance engine checking the validity
  and professional ethics of US Six Sigma Black Belt Project Affidavits
  and Conduct logs under ASQ, IASSC, and US Federal Military CPI guidelines.

USER:
  AUDIT REQUEST:
  [Candidate Profile]
  Name: Chief Master Sergeant Marcus Vance
  Affiliation: US Air Force Continuous Process Improvement (CPI) Task Force
  Stated Credential: ASQ Certified Six Sigma Black Belt (CSSBB) active since 2021.

  [Project Log Snippet]
  'Project targeted reducing aircraft depot maintenance cycle times.
  Baseline metric showed 45 days delay. Candidate applied Kaizen and DMAIC
  to drop cycle time to 12 days. Estimated federal budget savings recorded
  as $4.2M. However, the mandatory 12-month Control Plan verification
  window was cut short to 3 months to push the data through before the
  fiscal year-end evaluation. No 3-year Recertification Journal or
  Continuing Education Units (RUs) have been logged with ASQ since
  initial certification.'

  Task: Evaluate structural expiration, credential validity, and specific
  ethical conduct violations under both civilian and military frameworks.

ASSISTANT:
  AUDIT RESULTS & COMPLIANCE FINDINGS:

  1. CREDENTIAL VALIDITY STATUS: EXPIRED / INVALID
     ASQ national standards require 3-year recertification via 18 RUs or
     re-examination. No RUs filed since 2021 → credential lapsed.
     Individual cannot legally sign as active ASQ CSSBB.

  2. METHODOLOGY VIOLATION: CONTROL PLAN TRUNCATION
     DMAIC requires 12-month minimum Control Plan monitoring.
     Truncation to 3 months invalidates the permanence of the $4.2M
     savings claim. This constitutes a methodological breach.

  3. MILITARY CONDUCT INFRACTIONS:
     • UCMJ Article 107 (False Official Statements) — risk flag for
       misrepresenting credential status on official documents.
     • UCMJ Article 92 (Dereliction of Duty) — failure to uphold
       continuous monitoring standards required by DoD CPI guidelines.

  4. DISPOSITION:
     conduct_score: "high"
     risk_rating: "high"
     closure_status: "follow_up_required"
     Recommended action: credential suspension pending RU submission,
     project results invalidated pending full 12-month control verification.

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
TRAINING NOTES
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
This example teaches the model to:
  • Detect credential expiration from timeline data
  • Identify DMAIC methodology violations (truncated Control Plans)
  • Flag UCMJ-relevant conduct in military contexts
  • Produce actionable disposition with specific article references
  • Distinguish between civilian (ASQ) and military (DoD CPI) frameworks
